(:sigs :id "CARD-SIG-PROMOTE" :date "2026-11-14" :lead "Builtin signatures, arguments in this order:" :types "never written here: signatureSentence in asl/bench/gen/core.asl takes each type from the builtin registry, the asl-checker builtinSig row when there is one and else the :type of the asl/prelude/prelude.asn row, which is what asl '(:help :builtin NAME)' prints; a name the registry lacks fails the derivation" :order "the order of the rows is the order in the card" :pick "builtins the 30 reference solutions of asl/bench/gen/ref use and the card prose does not already type, plus = and charCode for the names models guessed (stringEqual?, isDigit, isLetter); listAny? and mapKeys of the lab table aslCardSig are dropped, no reference uses them")
(:sig :name "list" :note "so (list) is the empty list")
(:sig :name "str")
(:sig :name "=" :note "on strings and lists too")
(:sig :name "stringSplit" :note "text then separator")
(:sig :name "stringChars" :note "one-character strings")
(:sig :name "stringJoin")
(:sig :name "stringLength")
(:sig :name "stringEmpty?")
(:sig :name "stringContains?" :note "text then part")
(:sig :name "stringToInt64")
(:sig :name "stringFromInt64")
(:sig :name "charCode" :note "of the first character")
(:sig :name "map")
(:sig :name "filter")
(:sig :name "fold")
(:sig :name "listAll?")
(:sig :name "listReverse")
(:sig :name "listAppend")
(:sig :name "listDrop")
(:sig :name "listTake")
(:sig :name "listLast")
(:sig :name "listMax")
(:sig :name "listContains?")
(:sig :name "mapEmpty" :note "called as (mapEmpty)")
(:sig :name "mapSet")
(:sig :name "mapGetOr")
(:sig :name "mapValues")
(:sig :name "mapPairs")
(:sig :name "mapFromPairs")
(:sig :name "pair")
(:sig :name "pairFirst")
(:sig :name "pairSecond")
(:sig :name "optionOr")
(:sig :name "optionToResult")
